Small wave y = a exp(ikx) on the straight river (derived):
 dy/dt = -k^2 y (1 - P/(1+ik))
 growth rate  sigma(k) = k^2 (P - 1 - k^2) / (1 + k^2)      (grows for k^2 < P-1)
 drift speed  c(k)     = P k^2 / (1 + k^2), downstream (+x)
 check of ref.c: P=3, k=2pi*32/200=1.0053: theory sigma=0.4973, omega=c*k=1.5159; program 0.4966, 1.5126.
